{"content":[{"c":["TIPHSAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. City on the northeastern boundary of Solomon’s empire (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.24","r":"1Kgs.4.24","rawR":"1Kgs.4.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.24","value":"1Kgs.4.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:24"},"). It is most likely identified with Thapsacus, a town mentioned frequently in Greek and Roman texts. Though its precise location is unknown, it was an important trading center on the Euphrates River that dominated an east-west caravan route and also served as a northern terminal for river traffic."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. KJV rendering of Tappuah, one of the towns conquered by Menahem after he deposited Shallum in Samaria (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.15.16","r":"2Kgs.15.16","rawR":"2Kgs.15.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.15.16","value":"2Kgs.15.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 15:16"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=TappuahPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"TappuahPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"TappuahPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Tappuah (Place) #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Tiphsah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.24","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.24","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.24"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 15:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.15.16","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.15.16","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.15.16"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"115d98ba65c4faa04e11c4d6f1deaddf1602ea1e096cf05e121b564eca30ea4b","sourceItemName":"Tiphsah","sourceItemOrder":171,"sourceMember":"Articles/T.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Tiphsah","product":"TyndaleO